#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/migrations/dependencies.rst:87
msgid "What does this mean for me?"
msgstr "Hvad betyder dette for dig?"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/migrations/dependencies.rst:89
msgid ""
"You must specify all dependencies that the current Migration has, but not "
"any that the dependencies list as dependencies for their own installation."
msgstr ""
"Du skal angive alle afhængigheder, som den aktuelle migrering har, men ikke "
"dem, som afhængighederne selv angiver som afhængigheder for deres egen "
"installation."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/migrations/dependencies.rst:92
msgid ""
"This means that ``migration_5`` doesn't need to list ``migration_1`` through"
" ``migration_4`` as a dependency, only ``migration_3`` and ``migration_4`` "
"because those Migrations already require ``migration_1`` and "
"``migration_2``."
msgstr ""
"Dette betyder, at ``migration_5`` ikke behøver at angive ``migration_1`` til"
" ``migration_4`` som afhængighed, kun ``migration_3`` og ``migration_4``, "
"fordi disse migreringer allerede kræver ``migration_1`` og ``migration_2``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/migrations/dependencies.rst:96
msgid ""
"This also means that the desired order of operations is preserved. In the "
"above example, ``migration_4`` modifies the feature in ``migration_2`` and "
"must be applied after ``migration_2`` is installed. Similarly, in the above "
"example, ``migration_5`` is the release of 1.0.1, which requires both of the"
" two new features to be installed before it is 1.0.1."
msgstr ""
"Dette betyder også, at den ønskede rækkefølge af operationer bevares. I "
"eksemplet ovenfor ændrer ``migration_4`` funktionen i ``migration_2`` og "
"skal anvendes, efter at ``migration_2`` er installeret. Ligeledes er "
"``migration_5`` i eksemplet ovenfor udgivelsen af 1.0.1, som kræver, at "
"begge de to nye funktioner er installeret, før det er 1.0.1."
